  "commonEnable": "Enable",
  "commonTurnOn": "Turn on",
  "settingsPlayerLockExemptDialogTitle": "Enable double tap when locked",
  "settingsPlayerLockExemptDialogBody": "Once enabled, double-tapping the screen pauses or plays while the controls are locked.\n\nOnly this single gesture is exempted: swipe left/right to seek, swipe up/down for volume and brightness, and long-press for speed still do not work while locked; a single tap to show the unlock button is unaffected either.\n\nLocking exists to prevent accidental touches, so keep it off if your video pauses by accident in a pocket or bag.",
  "settingsPlayerGravityDialogTitle": "Turn on rotate UI with gravity",
  "settingsPlayerGravityDialogBody": "Requires both conditions:\n1. 'Auto-rotate' is enabled in the system settings;\n2. 'Video orientation' on this page is set to 'Follow video orientation'.\n\nWith both met, turning this on makes the player follow the phone orientation (portrait when held upright, landscape when turned sideways). If they are not met, playback still follows 'Video orientation' and this switch has no effect.\n\n'Always portrait / Always landscape' are explicit choices and are not affected by this switch.",
  "settingsPlayerGpuNextWarning": "Super resolution will be unavailable after enabling;\ntry software decoding to play Dolby Vision videos.\n\nContinue?",
  "settingsPlayerVulkanWarning": "Video output will prefer Vulkan rendering and new contexts are no longer limited to OpenGL ES.\n\nIf the device or driver does not support it, it falls back to OpenGL automatically with no black screen.\n\nNote: with the standard kernel, the MediaCodec direct path only works with OpenGL, so with Vulkan enabled 'HW+' goes straight to hardware copy (no direct path attempt).\n\nTakes effect after restarting the player (reopening the video).",
